+# Numeric admission and scheduling oracles
+
+Positive manual primary-spec trace, checked 2026-10-27. A concerns false dependency edges; B concerns missing scheduling. Neither asserts the disputed self-font numeric-cycle result.
+
+Registered values undergo complete grammar validation at computed-value time; registered providers substitute their computed result. Non-inheriting invalid declarations use their own registered initial value. Alternatives select the first matching component; multiplied syntaxes compute every admitted member. Thus a partial number list containing 1em is rejected, while a later valid numeric math member must also be computed. [PropertiesAPI computation](https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/#calculation-of-computed-values), [substitution](https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/#substitution), [syntax strings](https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/#syntax-strings), [complete grammar matching](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-syntax-3/#parse-grammar).
+
+A ready var primary excludes fallback substitution. A selected fallback still must satisfy the consuming registration. Therefore unused or rejected 1em cannot alter its consumer's font via that declaration. The scalar provider initial 3UNIT converts to consumer 3, distinct from incorrectly invalidating that consumer to its initial 7. [Variable replacement](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-variables-1/#replace-a-var-function), [property replacement](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-5/#property-replacement).
+
+Dimension-cancelling division yields a number; multiplication by one degree/second/dppx/percent yields that scalar. With independent target font 20→30px, em-based computation must yield 20→30 units. Integer results here are exact integers. Repetition computes each member, and registered substitution carries the computed scalar into consumers. These rules justify B's noncyclic expectations without defining a numeric self-font cycle policy. [Values 4 type checking](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#calc-type-checking), [computed math](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#calc-computed-value), [font units](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#font-relative-lengths).
+
+Percentage-to-number division remains excluded because its literal calibration failed. List comparisons normalize separators/whitespace only and compare every member. These traces do not prove parser/collector/effect correspondence to Lean. webspec-index is unavailable; this is a manually reviewed positive chain. Existing full primary snapshots are bound through REFERENCES; no fresh-download byte identity is claimed.
