+# Registered numeric A/B test partition
+
+The proposed landable A page has 104 required tests. A separate held research page has 16 B scheduling tests. The unchanged regression roster has 446 assertions and six reftests. There are 23 selected pages and 566 total testharness assertions. No paired runner or new native source-role binding is frozen here; the signing checkpoint and reviewed A source pins must precede that capsule.
+
+Install only candidate/testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-properties-values-api/registered-numeric-selected-dependencies.html with A. A-WPT.patch adds that single page. The held/ page is research input and must not be included in A's native+WPT commit. All 104 A tests must pass. B remains active work; compare its exact original/candidate observations rather than requiring it to turn green or editing expected metadata.
+
+The partition follows actual baseline evidence. The old 58 tests had 38 PASS/20 FAIL. Exactly three failing scheduling cases move to B: direct numeric division, current lh and inverse em. The other 55 remain in A (38 PASS/17 FAIL). Unregistered-provider-introduced math, root units, viewport and container controls really passed and remain A preservation controls. PRIOR58-PARTITION.json maps all 58 identities exactly once with actual original messages.
+
+A adds 45 calibrated breadth triplet rows:30 direct and 15 scalar-provider rows, excluding percentage-to-number conversion. Their 15 literal calibrations passed;30 fallback rows disagreed. Four new list admission controls cover two multi-member literals and two complete-list rejections; these still need a fresh original run. A total is 55+45+4=104.
+
+B has 3 old cases,6 direct scalar math cases,5 typed-provider math cases and 2 later-list mutations. Every held callback collects both mutation snapshots before assertions and embeds them in its observed= failure message. The future assessor must compare those messages with statuses/expectations/intermittents, detecting  FAIL→different- FAIL value changes. Report any A-induced B change instead of silently relabeling it. B total is 16. These noncyclic cases have sound proposed oracles but are outside A's repair promise.
+
+EXCLUDED-PERCENTAGE-DIVISION.json retains all four diagnostic rows. The literal percentage provider computed 5% while its number consumer computed initial 7; this is not rounding. Direct percentage registration, fallback and math remain covered. Percentage-to-number division is not a required pass until its separate calibration is resolved.
+
+The pinned pending 76-case registered-numeric-relative-units.html contains 72 noncyclic sign()-based scalar cases (24 absolute controls and 48 em/lh cases), plus 4 length controls. Target font 10px and line-height 12px are fixed; this snapshot contains zero self-font-cycle cases. PENDING76-OVERLAP.json lists all names and its hash. It overlaps B's context-computation issue family, adds sign/inheritance coverage and is not 76 new bug discoveries. It is not silently imported into this roster. The disputed self-font result remains in the separate observation artifact.
+
+historical/prior58.html preserves the previous page exactly; historical/proposed-combined-breadth62.html retains the unexecuted intermediate combined proposal. Neither is selected. Sealed fixture/capsule-v2 remain unchanged. Standalone breadth used a fresh default profile, not WPT preferences, so this genuine repartitioned WPT needs a fresh original baseline.
+
+The 21 existing regression manifest entries, resources, headers and metadata remain unchanged. A/B pages have no metadata overrides. The future capsule must retain full source/index/nested-repository preservation, caller-bound epoch and frozen HEAD, phase BuildID/binary bindings, compiled-role guards and owned-process cleanup.
